1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,177
Finly found a 967.11 percent consumed return and refused to trade it.

2
00:00:05,177 --> 00:00:08,196
That sentence is the product in miniature:

3
00:00:08,196 --> 00:00:13,373
a trading agent should be judged not only by what it finds,

4
00:00:13,373 --> 00:00:16,824
but by what it is willing to reject.

5
00:00:17,144 --> 00:00:21,336
In the consumed replay from January second,

6
00:00:21,336 --> 00:00:25,528
twenty thirteen through August twenty-seventh, twenty twenty-six,

7
00:00:25,528 --> 00:00:30,917
G4 returned 967.11 percent, versus 580.82 percent for SPY,

8
00:00:30,917 --> 00:00:36,307
after modeled five-basis-point one-way costs. The result was tempting.

9
00:00:36,307 --> 00:00:41,696
It was also selected after the history was visible.

10
00:00:42,016 --> 00:00:43,679
Finly denied promotion.

11
00:00:43,679 --> 00:00:47,559
The Deflated Sharpe probability was 3.75 percent,

12
00:00:47,559 --> 00:00:51,993
and the worst familywise-adjusted p-value was 37.18 percent.

13
00:00:51,993 --> 00:00:54,210
The chart remains visible,

14
00:00:54,210 --> 00:00:59,752
but it never received authority and cannot support a forecast.

15
00:01:00,072 --> 00:01:04,634
Production version one is the deliberately boring answer.

16
00:01:04,634 --> 00:01:07,485
In the consumed next-open study,

17
00:01:07,485 --> 00:01:13,757
it returned 15.39 percent at five basis points per traded leg,

18
00:01:13,757 --> 00:01:17,748
and 10.56 percent at twenty-five basis points.

19
00:01:17,748 --> 00:01:22,310
SPY returned 33.52 percent. At five basis points,

20
00:01:22,310 --> 00:01:29,722
Finly's annualized volatility was 8.12 percent and maximum drawdown was minus 5.45 percent.

21
00:01:29,722 --> 00:01:35,424
It was positive and risk-controlled. It did not beat SPY.

22
00:01:35,744 --> 00:01:37,957
That restraint is architectural.

23
00:01:37,957 --> 00:01:42,383
The model may interpret bounded evidence, explain uncertainty,

24
00:01:42,383 --> 00:01:47,915
or veto. Deterministic code owns exposure, order fields, maximum loss,

25
00:01:47,915 --> 00:01:53,447
and the final permit decision. A disagreement returns no trade;

26
00:01:53,447 --> 00:01:57,320
the model never writes the Alpaca payload.

27
00:01:57,640 --> 00:02:00,977
The interface keeps those evidence classes visible.

28
00:02:00,977 --> 00:02:04,315
Judges can inspect a positive production ledger,

29
00:02:04,315 --> 00:02:06,222
a rejected retrospective strategy,

30
00:02:06,222 --> 00:02:10,512
and two zero-outcome future tests on the same page.

31
00:02:10,512 --> 00:02:15,280
Finly does not hide the hard sentence in a footnote.

32
00:02:15,600 --> 00:02:19,909
Claims move from past to future only through a new test.

33
00:02:19,909 --> 00:02:23,434
A larger backtest never upgrades its own evidence class,

34
00:02:23,434 --> 00:02:26,568
and a prettier chart does not create authority.

35
00:02:26,888 --> 00:02:31,844
Attempts 115 and 116 are publicly registered future-only tests.

36
00:02:31,844 --> 00:02:35,149
As of August thirtieth, twenty twenty-six,

37
00:02:35,149 --> 00:02:40,656
each has zero observed outcomes; neither supports a performance claim.

38
00:02:40,656 --> 00:02:43,960
Registration makes the next claim falsifiable.

39
00:02:43,960 --> 00:02:47,264
It does not manufacture a result.

40
00:02:47,584 --> 00:02:50,586
That is Finly: publish the tempting result,

41
00:02:50,586 --> 00:02:53,159
reject what has not earned authority,

42
00:02:53,159 --> 00:02:55,732
and make the next claim falsifiable.

43
00:02:55,732 --> 00:03:00,449
Let AI interpret more and authorize less. The bull has horns;

44
00:03:00,449 --> 00:03:03,880
the llama still does not get the keys.
